(BAS-21 - without a blank line after the body, every following statement
 is absorbed into the function body, so the program silently does nothing:
 exit 0, no output. `greet.` here becomes a recursive call inside greet's
 own body, and nothing ever calls greet from the top level.
 Also covers: BAS-20 (the period ending `Print "hi".` closes only the
 innermost clause, so it does NOT close the function) and BAS-23 (the
 compiler warns at compile time - it is not silent about the cause, only
 the runtime is). The warning, which is compiler stderr and so not part of
 the recorded runtime output, reads:
   warning: Function 'greet' is still open at end of file: its body reached
   EOF with no closing blank line. ...
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-21.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   (exit 0)
)
To greet.
    Print "hi".
greet.
Print "top".
